# This repository versions the project's *thinking* — the cookbook, the journal,
# the lessons, the knowledge base, the backlog and the planning documents.
#
# It deliberately does not version:
#
#   - the Starting Kit itself, which is its own git repository
#   - anything large, regenerable, or downloaded
#   - anything holding a secret
#
# The knowledge base was unversioned until 2026-08-10, which meant twenty-nine
# lessons, the cookbook and the backlog had no history and no backup: one bad
# edit from gone. The code had been protected since the first day.

# The Starting Kit is its own repository, with its own history.
workspace/starting-kit/

# Backups hold database dumps and copies of .env — secrets, by definition.
workspace/.backups/

# A downloaded Node runtime and a build-tools installer. Regenerable, and large.
workspace/.toolchain/

# Candidate codebases kept for reference and the archives they came from.
open-mercato-main/
skills-main/
Platform/
*.zip

# Scratch space.
workspace/attic/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
copy-aissistant-reparsepoints.ps1
verify-aissistant-copy.ps1
aissistant-package/
aissistant-package-exact/

# Server credentials. Three files naming hosts and connection details.
# They were untracked, but nothing stopped `git add -A` from committing them —
# this file never named the folder. It does now. (Checked 2026-10-03.)
keys/

# A 30 MB archive of a host tree that contains a .env. Large, and a secret.
# The rule above already says large and secret things are not versioned; this
# file simply never matched any pattern. (Checked 2026-10-03.)
*.tgz

# A document from the SIBLING project, copied into this root. It is not ours:
# it is byte-identical to konsult/aissistant-package/documentation/cursor/companai.md
# and it reads as if it were a vision statement for our product. Left in place so
# it can be read and judged, but it must never be committed. See library/ai/README.md.
companai.md

# The Hermes runtime source, extracted into the library for reading. 17,201 files
# of somebody else's code (the 2026-10-03 note said 17,570 — re-measured 2026-10-16).
# The rule at the top of this file already excludes
# vendored code; this is the largest instance of it, and the one most likely to be
# committed by accident. (Checked 2026-10-03; count corrected 2026-10-16.)
library/ai/hermes-agent-main/

# The SAME Hermes runtime source ALSO sits at the repository root — in FOUR extracts
# side by side. The PINNED copy is `hermes-agent-main/` (revision db44c462…, 19,728
# files, digest 07ee857b…; see development/HERMES-PIN.md). `hermes-agent-main-newer/`
# is the PREVIOUS pin (revision 3569e846…, 18,248 files), renamed aside by the owner
# on 2026-10-15; `hermes-agent-main-older/` (17,367 files) is a superseded extract.
# The rule above already excludes vendored code; the bare name never matched the
# sibling copies, so they showed up as untracked and could have been swept in by a
# wildcard add. NOTE a bare name is NOT a prefix glob: `hermes-agent-main/` does NOT
# match `hermes-agent-main-newer/`, which is why EACH copy needs its own line.
# (Checked 2026-10-05; extended 2026-10-12 when the pin moved to the root; the
# `-newer` line added 2026-10-16 — the owner's rename left an 18,248-file tree
# untracked and NOT ignored, `git check-ignore` → NOT IGNORED.)
hermes-agent-main/
hermes-agent-main-newer/
hermes-agent-main-older/

# TAKEN, 2026-10-04 — the owner said yes. The hand-written parts are versioned;
# the copies are ignored. This supersedes the 2026-10-03 note below, which left
# the decision open on purpose.
#
# VERSIONED (ours, small, not rebuildable from anywhere): library/analysis/,
# library/development/, library/INDEX.md, library/PROVENANCE.md,
# library/MANIFEST.txt, library/.build_library.py, library/canonical-*.md,
# library/ai/README.md, library/ai/ai-first/, library/ai/tiny_models/, and the
# loose *.md files in library/ai/.
#
# ADDED 2026-10-05: `analysis/` and `llama/` at the repository root are also
# VERSIONED. Both are our own authored analysis (the earlier Hermes / Starting Kit
# study, and the eight documents the model-layer design was built from), small, and
# not rebuildable. The development documents cite them, so a clone without them had
# broken citations. Nothing here names them, which is why they were untracked.
#
# IGNORED, by the rules that follow this comment:
#   - the 16 numbered shelves (01-.. to 16-..): byte-for-byte copies of material
#     on E:, and .build_library.py rebuilds them deterministically. Do NOT put
#     anything hand-written inside a numbered shelf — the script deletes it.
#   - library/ai/hermes-agent-main/ and its .zip: another product's source, 17,570
#     files and an 88 MB archive.
#   - library/ai/hermes-docs/: 32 MB of the SIBLING project's documentation.
#
# CORRECTION — the 2026-10-03 note was wrong on one point and it matters. It said
# `library/ai/ai-first/` and `library/ai/hermes-docs/` are "regenerable by the
# build script". They are NOT. The script's PRESERVE set is {"ai", "analysis"}: it
# skips `ai/` entirely and has no source for it. So `ai-first/` is ignored as a
# *copy* — it is byte-identical to material on E: — and not because it can be
# rebuilt. The consequence, stated plainly: **ignoring it means it has no
# history.** That is accepted for a copy of an external source, and it is exactly
# why `ai/README.md`, which is ours and explains the split, IS versioned.
#
# The lesson at the top of this file — the knowledge base had no history and no
# backup, one bad edit from gone — no longer applies to `library/analysis/`.
library/[0-9][0-9]-*/
library/ai/hermes-agent-main.zip
library/ai/hermes-docs/

# The upstream Open Mercato documentation site, copied in on 2026-08-07: 471 files,
# 63 MB. It is upstream's docs content, not ours — the project's own position
# (where_we_left.md item B) is that upstream's docs must not ship under our name.
# Kept on disk for reference; not tracked. (Added 2026-10-05.)
library/kit-docs/

# Hyper-V build artefacts for the Coolify hosting environment. Large, regenerable,
# and one of them is a secret: the cloud-init seed carries the VM's credentials.
# A 4 GB Ubuntu ISO, the seed ISO, and a dynamically-expanding VHDX. None of this
# belongs in a repository of the project's thinking. (Added 2026-10-04 with
# library/development/PLAN-coolify-laptop-implementation.md.)
vms/

# Upstream Paperclip, extracted from paperclip-master.zip on 2026-10-05 (8,300 files,
# 132 MB; the zip lists 9,056 *entries* — 756 are folders). Reference material for the
# agent/task study. Not our code, not tracked.
library/ai/paperclip-master/

# One place for the scattered source documents the study reads — created 2026-10-05 at
# the owner's request. The copies (317 markdown files from upstream Paperclip's doc set)
# are somebody else's documentation, so they follow the 2026-10-04 rule above: the copies
# are ignored, the register is not. README.md is the register and is tracked.
library/ai/source-docs/*
!library/ai/source-docs/README.md

# The D2-gap measurement's raw JSON dump and its stderr. `analysis/d2-gap/measure.js --json`
# prints the JSON to stdout and any warnings to stderr; `d2.json` / `d2.err` are just those
# streams redirected to files (`d2.json` is ~95 KB). Both are regenerable on demand from the
# tool, and nothing cites them — the AUTHORED analysis next to them,
# `analysis/d2-gap/FINDINGS.md`, is the thing that is tracked and quoted. Adding the rules
# rather than the files keeps a large machine dump out of a repository whose stated purpose
# is to version the project's *thinking* (see the header of this file). (Added 2026-10-07
# while closing out the `business_rules` fix — it surfaced as untracked and would otherwise
# have been swept in by a `git add -A`. `d2.err` added the same way while closing out
# `inbox_ops`.)
analysis/d2-gap/d2.json
analysis/d2-gap/d2.err

# Extracted platform source trees for the architecture studies. Huge, regenerable
# from the .zip files sitting next to them (which are themselves ignored above).
library/architecture/platforms/_extracted/

# A SECOND copy of the Hermes forensics study, placed inside the workshop folder so
# the architecture stage reads as one tree. The original `library/hermes-forensics/`
# is already versioned (14 files); a duplicate adds no history and would silently
# drift from the original. The owner chose to ignore the copy rather than track it
# (2026-10-15). NOTE a trailing slash matches the directory only, which is what we
# want — a bare name would also catch any future `hermes-forensics-*` sibling.
library/architecture/hermes-forensics/
